Why the split
-------------
The DK-QUAKE / ARIS-68 protocol (HID interface IDs, frame format, opcodes,
checksum, and the touch/knob/RGB-ring semantics) was reverse-engineered from
DK-Suite V0.4.35 by the Bedrock Panel project (github.com/TeeJS/bedrock-panel),
which released it under PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0 at the vendor's request
(the vendor described the protocol as restricted for commercial use, with
non-commercial use permitted). This repository ports that driver to run under
Linux/Quickshell rather than Electron/Windows; the ported files carry the same
license and the same "Required Notice" the original requires you to preserve
(see `daemon/LICENSE`). This may be relaxed to a permissive license if
explicit written commercial permission is obtained from the protocol holders.

Everything else in this repository — the Quickshell UI, the daemon's own
process/IPC plumbing, and all ops/config scaffolding — is wholly original work
built for this project and is MIT-licensed.

